WEBVTT

NOTE
Narration and scene timings are sourced from
Plenum Briefing/Plenum_Platform_Explainer_Video_Script.md.
The authored narration ends at 01:28; the full media continues to 02:28.

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
Fractured Order is a live economic statecraft simulation.
Multiple actors interpret a changing strategic environment,
make decisions, communicate, and adapt across several phases of play.

00:10.000 --> 00:16.000
A complex simulation can quickly become difficult to coordinate.
Decisions, communications, timing, facilitation, adjudication,
and observation may be scattered across disconnected tools
and informal processes.

00:16.000 --> 00:22.000
That makes it harder to know what is current,
who owns the next action, and how an event changed the course of play.

00:22.000 --> 00:28.000
Plenum addresses this problem by providing a shared
browser-based operating layer for the exercise.

00:28.000 --> 00:34.000
It connects participant workspaces with the control-cell tools needed
to run, monitor, document, and review the simulation.

00:34.000 --> 00:39.000
Each role has a defined responsibility within the shared session state.

00:39.000 --> 00:43.000
The Scribe records orientations, forecasts, actions, proposals,
responses, and Requests for Information.

00:43.000 --> 00:46.500
The Facilitator supports team discussion, reviews received proposals,
and helps manage interaction.

00:46.500 --> 00:49.500
The Notetaker captures team dynamics, alliances, turning points,
and the decision process behind the outcome.

00:49.500 --> 00:52.000
White Cell manages timing, phases, updates, review, and adjudication,
while the Game Master administers sessions and exports the evidence.

00:52.000 --> 00:59.000
During Strategic Orientation and Moves One through Three,
Plenum links decisions to timing, communication, review,
adjudication, and consequences.

00:59.000 --> 01:06.000
Teams can record what they choose, why they choose it,
how they coordinate, and how they adapt when new information arrives.

01:06.000 --> 01:12.000
The result is more than a live interface.
It is a structured record of the exercise:

01:12.000 --> 01:18.000
what teams believed, what they decided, what information they received,
how they interacted, and how outcomes developed over time.

01:18.000 --> 01:23.000
Plenum does not replace strategic judgment or facilitation.
It gives Statecraft Simulations Group the operational structure
to focus on them.

01:23.000 --> 01:28.000
It turns a complex exercise into a coordinated,
observable, and reviewable simulation.
